<section class="journal-intro"><div class="container journal-intro-inner"><span class="journal-intro-icon">✦</span><div><span class="eyebrow">THE WARDROBE GUIDE</span><p>A useful wardrobe is not simply a collection of clothes. It is a group of pieces that work together, suit the occasions in your life and help you feel comfortable and confident. Whether you prefer elegant dresses, relaxed skirts or smart everyday outfits, a little planning can make choosing what to wear easier. This style guide explores practical ways to think about clothing, fit, colour and care. It is general fashion guidance; check the current ANILLAH CLOSET catalogue for products and availability.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="journal-articles"><div class="container"><div class="journal-section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">THE STYLE PLAYBOOK</span><h2>Find your next outfit idea</h2><p>Practical notes for getting dressed with more ease and personality.</p></div><div class="journal-card-grid"><article class="journal-card journal-berry"><div class="journal-card-number">01</div><div class="journal-card-copy"><span class="journal-kicker">STYLE NOTE 01</span><h2>Start with the occasions you dress for</h2><p>Before buying something new, think about the activities that make up your week. You may need outfits for work, classes, family gatherings, church, celebrations, weekends or travel. Write down the occasions that matter most and identify the clothing that would be useful for each one. A versatile dress that can be styled with different shoes or accessories may serve more than one purpose. A skirt that works with a simple top can also create several combinations. Choose pieces that fit your actual routine rather than buying something only because it is fashionable for a moment.</p></div><span class="journal-card-mark" aria-hidden="true">✦</span></article><article class="journal-card journal-plum"><div class="journal-card-number">02</div><div class="journal-card-copy"><span class="journal-kicker">STYLE NOTE 02</span><h2>Choose colours that work together</h2><p>Colour can change the mood of an outfit. Neutral shades such as black, white, navy and beige are often easy to combine. Brighter colours, prints and patterns can add personality and become the focus of an outfit. You do not need to limit your wardrobe to neutrals. Instead, consider selecting a few colours that complement one another and that you enjoy wearing. When choosing a patterned skirt or dress, you can keep accessories simple or pick one colour from the pattern to repeat elsewhere in the outfit.</p></div><span class="journal-card-mark" aria-hidden="true">✦</span></article><article class="journal-card journal-gold"><div class="journal-card-number">03</div><div class="journal-card-copy"><span class="journal-kicker">STYLE NOTE 03</span><h2>Pay attention to fit and comfort</h2><p>A garment can look attractive on a hanger but feel different when worn. Check the fit around the shoulders, waist, bust, hips and length. Make sure you can sit, walk and move comfortably. If you are shopping online or enquiring through a boutique, ask for the garment measurements rather than relying on a size label alone. Sizing can vary between styles and manufacturers. Ask whether the item is stretchy, lined or fitted, and confirm the available sizes before placing an order. The most useful outfit is one that allows you to feel at ease throughout the day.</p></div><span class="journal-card-mark" aria-hidden="true">✦</span></article><article class="journal-card journal-violet"><div class="journal-card-number">04</div><div class="journal-card-copy"><span class="journal-kicker">STYLE NOTE 04</span><h2>Style dresses for different settings</h2><p>Dresses can be practical because one garment can form the foundation of an entire outfit. A simple dress may work for daytime with comfortable flats and a light bag. The same dress can look more formal with smart shoes, a jacket or carefully chosen jewellery. For an event, consider the venue, weather, dress code and how long you will be wearing the outfit. A flowing style may feel comfortable in warm weather, while a more structured design may suit a formal occasion. Always choose an outfit that feels appropriate to the event and comfortable for you.</p></div><span class="journal-card-mark" aria-hidden="true">✦</span></article><article class="journal-card journal-forest"><div class="journal-card-number">05</div><div class="journal-card-copy"><span class="journal-kicker">STYLE NOTE 05</span><h2>Make skirts easy to coordinate</h2><p>Skirts come in many lengths, shapes, fabrics and prints. A plain skirt can be paired with a patterned top, while a printed skirt can be balanced with a solid-colour blouse or T-shirt. Consider the proportions of the outfit: a tucked-in top can define the waist, while a longer or looser top creates a more relaxed silhouette. Think about footwear too. The same skirt may look different with trainers, sandals or formal shoes. Try combinations with clothes you already own before deciding what additional pieces you need.</p></div><span class="journal-card-mark" aria-hidden="true">✦</span></article><article class="journal-card journal-rose"><div class="journal-card-number">06</div><div class="journal-card-copy"><span class="journal-kicker">STYLE NOTE 06</span><h2>Look after your clothes</h2><p>Good clothing care helps garments remain wearable for longer. Read the care label before washing. Separate colours when necessary, use suitable detergents and avoid high heat when a fabric may shrink or become damaged. Store dresses and delicate garments on appropriate hangers, and fold heavier knitwear to help it keep its shape. Treat stains as soon as practical using a method suitable for the fabric. If an item requires special cleaning, follow the manufacturer's instructions or seek professional advice.</p></div><span class="journal-card-mark" aria-hidden="true">✦</span></article><article class="journal-card journal-berry"><div class="journal-card-number">07</div><div class="journal-card-copy"><span class="journal-kicker">STYLE NOTE 07</span><h2>Shop thoughtfully</h2><p>Before ordering, confirm the product name, price, size, colour, stock status and delivery arrangements with the seller. Ask about payment methods and the exchange or return policy. Keep a record of the order confirmation and any agreed delivery details. A product photograph is useful for seeing a style, but the seller should confirm that the photograph represents the item currently available. Do not assume that a displayed sample price or size is current without checking.</p></div><span class="journal-card-mark" aria-hidden="true">✦</span></article><article class="journal-card journal-plum"><div class="journal-card-number">08</div><div class="journal-card-copy"><span class="journal-kicker">STYLE NOTE 08</span><h2>Find pieces that feel like you</h2><p>Personal style develops over time. You can experiment with colour, prints, shapes and accessories while keeping comfort and practicality in mind. The goal is not to own the largest wardrobe; it is to choose clothes that suit your preferences and can be worn in ways that feel authentic. Explore the ANILLAH CLOSET collection, ask questions about fit and availability, and select pieces that make sense for your lifestyle. A thoughtful wardrobe makes getting dressed simpler and gives you more opportunities to enjoy the clothes you own.</p></div><span class="journal-card-mark" aria-hidden="true">✦</span></article></div><div class="journal-endnote"><span>YOUR STYLE, YOUR STORY</span><p>Explore the collection and choose pieces that feel like you.</p><a class="btn" href="shop.php">Explore the collection</a></div></div></section>
